# CODEOWNERS - the people who must approve a change to the files that judge a
# change. Built from plugins/productizer/skills/spec/templates/CODEOWNERS
# (B178). Never a bot: a bot's approval is not a person deciding.
#
# GitHub reads the first of .github/CODEOWNERS, CODEOWNERS and docs/CODEOWNERS
# that exists, and the last matching pattern wins. Keep these lines LAST, so no
# later pattern takes one of these files away from its owner, and never leave a
# pattern under them with no owner: that leaves its files approvable by anyone
# with write access.
#
# This file does nothing by itself. Branch protection (or a ruleset) on main
# must "Require review from Code Owners", and turning that on is the
# maintainer's step on GitHub; see
# plugins/productizer/skills/spec/references/stage-3-6-build.md, "Approval rules
# for an agent-authored change". The approval-rules check reads this file; it
# cannot read the settings.

/.claude/productizer/ @gitayg
/.github/workflows/ @gitayg
